  "body": "### Summary\nAs a user with the account sync on, I want a session check that only renewed my cookies' expiry dates to change nothing in the shared copy, so that no device ever sees \"new credentials\" where there are none. This is the source of the #1276 loop: #1385 stops its effect in the app (`takeOver`), the engine still produces the echo. Audit #1388, finding A1.\n\n### What happens (read at `dev-swift` `1685bcc`)\n1. Every valid check ends in `AccountsModel.persistSession` (`App/SwiftHFR/Accounts/AccountsModel.swift:218-220`, `:322-360`). HFR re-sends `md_user` / `md_passs` with a new expiry on every logged-in answer (HFR-PROTOCOL §6c, `R74`), so `stored == before` is false and `noteSyncChange(.refresh)` runs (`:349`).\n2. `AccountSync.localChange(.refresh)` stamps `credentialsAt = now` (`Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRStorage/AccountSync/AccountSync.swift:107-109`) and reconciles: the merged envelope differs from the item, so the **synchronizable Keychain item is rewritten** (`:309-312`).\n3. On every other device, the next reconcile (each foreground, `AppLifecycle.swift:97-101`) finds the remote copy newer: `AccountSyncMerge.replaced` compares whole `Account` values, dates included (`AccountSyncMerge.swift:58-62`; a tie keeps the remote, `:67-71`) and reports the account `replaced`.\n\n### Failing scenario and count\n- One device, one account, sync on: **1 iCloud Keychain write per valid check** (each launch), for a change that is only dates.\n- Two devices: each launch of A makes B report `replaced` at its next foreground. Before #1385 that is 1 profile check + 1 home page + up to 4 list reloads on B, whose own write-back then does the same to A. With #1385 the take-over is skipped only while B's session is `valid` with the same login; `restored` / `checkFailed` sessions still adopt, signal and check.\n- A copy dated ahead of this device's clock: the #1276 loop itself (13 checks, 36 requests in 2.7 s).\n\n### Proposed fix\n- In the engine, a `.refresh` whose login identity (`md_user`, `md_passs`, `md_id` values) equals what the copy holds does not move `credentialsAt` and does not rewrite the item; `replaced` compares the login identity, not the dates.\n- Keep #1385's app-side guard as the second line.\n- Test (Linux, `HFRStorageTests`): two `AccountSync` over one in-memory item; a refresh with new expiries only → `itemWritten == false`, the other device's reconcile → `replaced.isEmpty`; a real re-login still propagates.\n\n### Acceptance\n- An expiry-only refresh writes nothing to the synchronizable item and is never reported as `replaced`.\n- A re-login on one device is still adopted once by the other.\n\nSessions and credentials: merged by the core orchestrator or the maintainer (AGENTS.md §8).\n\nRefs #1388, #1276, #1385.",
