   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp**: one more case for this issue, from the Fable round 2 review of #1385 (non-blocking there): when the copy that wins the device's own write-back push holds a different `md_passs`, the store takes it while the live session keeps its own (`AccountsModel.swift:467` @ 40391f5e, seen in a probe); a later foreground reconcile then has nothing to report, so the session only picks it up at the next cold launch. Needs a copy dated ahead that changes between the launch reconcile and the first check's push.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
