   "body": "/claim cloud/i1390-opus\n\nPlan:\n- Engine (`HFRStorage/AccountSync`): a `.refresh` whose login identity (`md_user`, `md_passs`, `md_id` values) equals the synced copy's keeps the copy's `credentialsAt` and does not rewrite the synchronizable item.\n- `AccountSyncMerge.replaced` compares login identity, not cookie dates.\n- Clock-ahead case (comment 7221677106): look at option (b), same identity → keep the later expiries in the device store; a real re-login is clamped past the remote stamp (option a) if it stays in scope, otherwise a follow-up issue.\n- TDD in `HFRStorageTests`: two `AccountSync` over one in-memory item, expiry-only refresh → no item write and `replaced` empty on the other device; re-login still adopted once. Seen red first.\n- Keep #1385's app-side guard; draft PR, Fable adversarial review, `compile-check` for the final run.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
